{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.HydrogenPartitionFunction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.HydrogenPartitionFunction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.MathConstants","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.partition_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.partition_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L104-L132","doc":"The partition function is monotone in j_max: adding more angular\nmomentum modes can only increase Z (all Boltzmann factors are positive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hydrogen_partition_ground_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hydrogen_partition_ground_pos","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L91-L102","doc":"**Hydrogen heat capacity** at low temperature (high β):\nthe partition function with only j = 0 equals 1, which is positive.\nThis shows the ground state is non-degenerate and Z > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.rotationalPartitionFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.rotationalPartitionFunction","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**Rotational partition function** for a single hydrogen atom.\nz_rot = Σ_{j=0}^{j_max} [2j+1]_q · exp(-β · [j]_q[j+1]_q · ℏ_q).\nParameterised by the maximum angular momentum j_max. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ground_state_contribution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ground_state_contribution","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L72-L78","doc":"**The j = 0 contribution** to the partition function is 1\n(degeneracy [1]_q = 1 times Boltzmann factor exp(0) = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.boltzmann_ground_state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.boltzmann_ground_state","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**Boltzmann factor at j = 0**: exp(-β · J²(0) · ℏ_q) = exp(0) = 1.\nSince J²(0) = 0, the exponent vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.sq_ne_one_of_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.sq_ne_one_of_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L60-L63","doc":"When q > 1, we have q² ≠ 1 (needed for qDegeneracy lemmas). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qDegeneracy_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qDegeneracy_zero","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L42-L58","doc":"[1]_q = 1 for all nonzero q ≠ ±1.\nProof: [1]_q = (q - q⁻¹)/(q - q⁻¹) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qDegeneracy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qDegeneracy","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L38-L40","doc":"**q-degeneracy**: the number of states at spin j is [2j+1]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qAngularMomentum_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qAngularMomentum_zero","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L32-L36","doc":"At j = 0, the angular momentum vanishes: [0]_q · [1]_q = 0.\nThis is because [0]_q = (q⁰ - q⁻⁰)/(q - q⁻¹) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qAngularMomentum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qAngularMomentum","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hydrogen-partition-function.lean#L25-L30","doc":"**q-angular momentum eigenvalue** J²_q(j) = [j]_q · [j+1]_q.\nThis is the Casimir of SU_q(2) at spin j. ","signatureChunk":0}]}